# Share this session with your team

`multiplayer-cli` turns one AI session into a room several people share. Everyone
sees the same transcript, and nothing reaches the model until the room agrees.

## Start it

```bash
mpx share
```

If `mpx` is missing (package not on npm yet):

```bash
npx github:fathyshalaby/multiplayer-cli share
```

For a dry run with no API key: `mpx share --backend echo --policy pair`

Then **give the user the link verbatim**. Do not shorten it — the `#t=…` fragment
is the room key. Do not paste the link anywhere yourself.

Whoever opens the link gets a browser seat or a terminal join command. Neither
needs an API key — only the host does.

## In the session

Bare text is a proposal. `/y` approves, `/n <reason>` vetoes, `/say` talks to
the room without spending a turn. `/help` lists commands.

## Cursor editor seat

Install the extension from a built `.vsix` (`npm run build:extension` then package
in `extension/`). Command palette: **Share this folder as a session**.

See `skills/multiplayer/SKILL.md` for relay, policy, racing, and splitting.
